WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.617
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:09.396
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:17.713
Unit nineteen: C1 Advanced: Listening. Today you will follow complex talks and identify attitude, opinion and implied meaning.

4
00:00:18.013 --> 00:00:20.572
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:24.662
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:26.611
Implication.

7
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:30.208
Implication means a suggested meaning.

8
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:32.503
Listen for implication.

9
00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:35.862
Your turn. Say: Implication.

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.782
Implication.

11
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:41.425
Attitude.

12
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.648
Attitude means how someone feels.

13
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.750
What is her attitude?

14
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.700
Your turn. Say: Attitude.

15
00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:53.533
Attitude.

16
00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:55.284
Hesitate.

17
00:00:56.283 --> 00:00:58.678
Hesitate means to pause because of doubt.

18
00:00:59.283 --> 00:01:01.225
He hesitated before answering.

19
00:01:01.817 --> 00:01:04.214
Your turn. Say: Hesitate.

20
00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:07.998
Hesitate.

21
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:09.705
Stress.

22
00:01:10.717 --> 00:01:13.343
Stress means extra emphasis on a word.

23
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.474
Listen for stress.

24
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:18.666
Your turn. Say: Stress.

25
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.780
Stress.

26
00:01:23.517 --> 00:01:24.611
Interviewer.

27
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:28.429
Interviewer means the person who asks questions.

28
00:01:29.017 --> 00:01:31.225
The interviewer asks about her career.

29
00:01:31.817 --> 00:01:34.411
Your turn. Say: Interviewer.

30
00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:38.233
Interviewer.

31
00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:39.845
Monologue.

32
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.651
Monologue means a long speech by one person.

33
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.750
Listen to the monologue.

34
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.049
Your turn. Say: Monologue.

35
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:52.913
Monologue.

36
00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:54.686
Paraphrase.

37
00:01:55.683 --> 00:01:58.647
Paraphrase means the same idea in other words.

38
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.087
The option is a paraphrase.

39
00:02:01.683 --> 00:02:04.579
Your turn. Say: Paraphrase.

40
00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:08.713
Paraphrase.

41
00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.230
Gist.

42
00:02:11.217 --> 00:02:12.798
Gist means the main meaning.

43
00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:14.721
Understand the gist.

44
00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:17.783
Your turn. Say: Gist.

45
00:02:20.633 --> 00:02:21.623
Gist.

46
00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:25.933
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.783 --> 00:02:29.619
Visal, what do C1 Listening tasks test?

48
00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:44.201
They test detailed understanding of extracts, a monologue with sentence completion, an interview and a multiple-matching task. You must follow opinions and attitudes that are often implied.

49
00:02:45.317 --> 00:02:47.502
How can I understand implied meaning?

50
00:02:48.617 --> 00:02:57.387
Listen to stress, pauses and tone. If a speaker hesitates before saying it was interesting, the real meaning may be negative.

51
00:02:58.483 --> 00:03:00.297
How do I avoid distractors?

52
00:03:01.383 --> 00:03:10.978
Do not choose the first option you hear. Wait for the whole idea, because speakers often mention a view and then correct or reject it.

53
00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.761
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.617 --> 00:03:18.810
Grammar focus: Strategy: whole idea, tone, paraphrase.

55
00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.309
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:21.017 --> 00:03:24.061
It was interesting, she said, with a pause that showed doubt.

57
00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:28.018
The speaker mentions both views but agrees with the second.

58
00:03:28.967 --> 00:03:36.251
Listen for tone, stress and pauses. Wait until the speaker finishes the whole idea and choose the option that paraphrases it.

59
00:03:37.017 --> 00:03:40.934
Be careful! Don't say: I take the tone at face value.

60
00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.828
Say: I listen for tone and pauses.

61
00:03:46.128 --> 00:03:47.629
Tone shows attitude.

62
00:03:48.433 --> 00:03:50.993
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:52.801
An Interview.

64
00:03:53.101 --> 00:03:56.146
An interviewer asks an architect about her new building.

65
00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:59.388
She says, It was... interesting, with a pause.

66
00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.340
The listener understands that she may have had problems.

67
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:06.820
She then explains that the budget was too small.

68
00:04:07.833 --> 00:04:10.204
The correct answer shows her real attitude.

69
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.348
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:16.183 --> 00:04:18.427
C1 Listening has blank parts.

71
00:04:18.727 --> 00:04:21.672
A, eight. B, four. C, one.

72
00:04:25.233 --> 00:04:26.966
The answer is B: four.

73
00:04:28.117 --> 00:04:30.650
A pause before 'interesting' may show blank.

74
00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:34.464
A, joy. B, fear of water. C, doubt.

75
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.883
The answer is C: doubt.

76
00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.748
You should not choose blank.

77
00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:48.025
A, the first option you hear. B, any option. C, an option.

78
00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:54.356
The answer is A: the first option you hear.

79
00:04:55.517 --> 00:04:57.272
Why was the building difficult?

80
00:04:57.572 --> 00:05:01.667
A, the colour. B, the budget was too small. C, the weather.

81
00:05:05.233 --> 00:05:08.057
The answer is B: the budget was too small.

82
00:05:09.217 --> 00:05:11.321
Correct answers often use a blank.

83
00:05:11.621 --> 00:05:15.286
A, copy. B, title. C, paraphrase.

84
00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:21.471
The answer is C: paraphrase.

85
00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:25.992
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:29.488
How do you listen for attitude in a C1 recording?

87
00:05:38.283 --> 00:05:39.969
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:40.269 --> 00:05:53.188
I listen to the speaker's stress, pauses and tone as well as the words. I wait for the whole idea before I choose an answer. The correct option is often a paraphrase of what the speaker says.

89
00:05:53.488 --> 00:05:55.441
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:02.439
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: whole idea, tone, paraphrase.

91
00:06:02.739 --> 00:06:07.945
Today's value is reflective awareness. Notice your own experience with care and honesty.

92
00:06:08.245 --> 00:06:10.747
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

93
00:06:11.047 --> 00:06:14.837
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

